# Testing rules

Owning doc: `plans/TEST_STRATEGY.md` (levels, cadence, thresholds, the T-xx catalogue, Definition of Done). Tools: ADR-019.

## Naming

- Every test traces to a T-xx from the catalogue. If your spec needs a new one, add it to the catalogue in the same PR.
- Python: mark with `@pytest.mark.t("T-55")` and name the function for the behaviour: `test_stale_approval_is_rejected`.
- TypeScript and Playwright: start the title with the ID: `test("T-44 compiler errors name the scene and field", …)`.
- Conformance scenarios keep their C-ID in the title too: `T-05 C05 approval bound to an old version is invalid`.

## Where tests live

| Level | Path |
|---|---|
| Backend unit, functional, conformance | `backend/tests/unit/`, `backend/tests/functional/`, `backend/tests/conformance/` |
| Agent mocked | `agent/tests/`; eval scenarios in `agent/evals/` (format in `agent.mdc`) |
| Media | `media/scenes/tests/`, `media/audio/tests/` |
| Web unit and component | `web/tests/` |
| Contract | `contracts/tests/` |
| Playwright | `e2e/smoke/`, `e2e/screens/` (T-15–T-30), `e2e/journeys/`, `e2e/conformance/`, `e2e/nfr/` |

## Rules

- Write the spec's listed tests first, covering every acceptance criterion including refusals, blockers and error classes.
- Deterministic: freeze time, seed randomness, no sleeps (wait on conditions), no order dependence.
- No real provider or network calls outside `make eval LIVE=1` and the weekly and milestone jobs. Use the adapter fakes; the fake identity provider only with `APP_ENV=test`.
- Functional tests use real PostgreSQL and the object store through Testcontainers, never SQLite or mocks of the database.
- Synthetic data only: the odd-squares fixture, the first three topics' fixtures, seeds from `make seed`. Never copy real channel or production data into a fixture.
- Live progress in UI tests comes from the recorded AG-UI streams in `docs/contracts/examples/agui/`.
- Screen tests cover every state in the screen's UI_DESIGN row, copy, the keyboard path and axe; visual baselines are updated only when you approved the change in the PR.
- Hypothesis for functions with input domains (demonstrations, budget arithmetic, hashing).
- Never weaken, skip or delete a test, eval, golden file or threshold to make a change pass. A flaky test is fixed or quarantined with an issue, never ignored.
- Never edit the criteria that judge a change (graders, goldens, thresholds) in the same PR that changes what they judge, unless the spec says so (C13).
